WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:06.051
Acceleration is how fast velocity changes: the gradient of a speed–time graph.

2
00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:10.151
A four newton push on a two kilogram trolley.

3
00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:18.905
Its speed rises two metres per second every second: two metres per second squared.

4
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:22.633
Now double the push to eight newtons.

5
00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:36.607
Double the net force, and the speed rises twice as fast.
